# REQUIRES: python-api
# A Python simulation at constant pressure in a triclinic cell, on the CPU
# (D[python-triclinic-npt], docs/python-segments.md), Inputs/python_dlpack_tilts.py:
# 403 waters in a rhombic dodecahedron with PME, in the deterministic mode.
# The barostat scales the tilts with the cell and the state of the host has
# them: a run in parts equals one run, a simulation continued from a
# checkpoint the one that wrote it; a commit of tilts through a writable
# borrow followed by steps under the barostat equals a simulation compiled
# from the committed state; a frame of the run is committed into the
# simulation that ran it; a part that the barostat fails leaves the cell of
# before with its tilts; 20 frames of the run are put into a second
# simulation. python-triclinic-npt-cli-*.test compare the run with
# `mdir run`.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_dlpack_tilts.py %S/Inputs/triclinic CPU npt %t | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: Double: at constant pressure the tilts follow the barostat (by {{[0-9.e-]+}} nm in 60 steps, the shape kept within 0e+00); a run in parts equals one run to the bit, and one continued from a checkpoint the run that wrote it
# CHECK: Double: a commit of tilts before the first step and 40 steps under the barostat, which moves the tilts by {{[0-9.e-]+}} nm, equal a simulation compiled from the committed state to the bit
# CHECK: Double: a frame of the run committed into the simulation that ran it, 20 steps later: the evaluation equals that of a simulation compiled from the frame to the bit, and the barostat goes on from its cell
# CHECK: Double: a part that the barostat fails after step {{[0-9]+}} leaves the cell of that step with its tilts
# CHECK: Double: 20 frames of a Python run at constant pressure (c_x from {{[0-9.]+}} to {{[0-9.]+}} nm) put into one simulation: the energies and the forces of each equal those of a simulation compiled from the frame
# CHECK: Mixed: at constant pressure the tilts follow the barostat (by {{[0-9.e-]+}} nm in 60 steps, the shape kept within 0e+00); a run in parts equals one run to the bit, and one continued from a checkpoint the run that wrote it
# CHECK: Mixed: a commit of tilts before the first step and 40 steps under the barostat, which moves the tilts by {{[0-9.e-]+}} nm, equal a simulation compiled from the committed state to the bit
# CHECK: Mixed: a frame of the run committed into the simulation that ran it, 20 steps later: the evaluation equals that of a simulation compiled from the frame to the bit, and the barostat goes on from its cell
# CHECK: Mixed: a part that the barostat fails after step {{[0-9]+}} leaves the cell of that step with its tilts
# CHECK: Mixed: 20 frames of a Python run at constant pressure (c_x from {{[0-9.]+}} to {{[0-9.]+}} nm) put into one simulation: the energies and the forces of each equal those of a simulation compiled from the frame
# CHECK: triclinic npt CPU passed
